Query: Fix the iframe loading bug in 
/home/kyle/projects/rogue-pachinko/tests/index.html.

ROOT CAUSE: Using iframe.src=url to load game HTML creates a cross-origin iframe
that cannot load /index.html reliably — GS ends up undefined. The URL resolution
with import.meta.url fails in non-module contexts.

YOUR TASK: In runAll() (lines 279-361 of tests/index.html), replace the iframe 
loading approach with srcdoc injection:

1. At the start of runAll(), BEFORE any iframe operations, fetch the game HTML:
   const resp = await fetch(GAME_SRC);
   const gameHtml = await resp.text();

2. Instead of: iframe.src = url.href; await load;
   Use: iframe.srcdoc = gameHtml; await new Promise(r => 
iframe.addEventListener('load', r, {once:true}));

3. Keep these EXACTLY as-is:
   - GAME_SRC = '/index.html' (line 45)
   - The gsCheck/GS-undefined handling (lines 290-315)
   - The seed/floor URL param logic (lines 283-285)
   - getTestFiles(), runSuiteInIframe(), buildTestWrapper() — do NOT touch these
   - The autorun trigger at the bottom

4. If the fetch fails, log error and fall back to iframe.src approach as a 
safety net.

Write the fixed tests/index.html to 
/home/kyle/projects/rogue-pachinko/tests/index.html
Run: node --check /home/kyle/projects/rogue-pachinko/tests/index.html
Do NOT use git commands. Do NOT open PRs.


